<body>
  <main class="pin-page">
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="eyebrow">Easy + Nourishing</div>
      <h1>Healthy Pregnancy Breakfast Ideas</h1>
      <p>
        Simple, balanced breakfast ideas that feel doable in real life — perfect for busy mornings,
        nausea days, and days when you just need something easy but filling.
      </p>
      <a class="cta" href="https://YOURDOMAIN.com/healthy-pregnancy-breakfast-ideas/">Read More</a>
    </section>

    <section class="image-wrap">
      <img src="https://YOURDOMAIN.com/pinterest-images/healthy-pregnancy-breakfast-ideas-pin-1.jpg" alt="Healthy Pregnancy Breakfast Ideas Pinterest Pin" />
    </section>

    <section class="content">
      <div class="intro-box">
        <strong>Chef’s Note:</strong> These breakfast ideas are built around real-life needs:
        protein, fiber, healthy fats, easy prep, and comfort. The goal is not perfection — it’s
        finding easy meals you will actually eat.
      </div>

      <h2 class="section-title">6 Healthy Pregnancy Breakfast Ideas</h2>

      <div class="recipe-grid">
        <article class="recipe-card">
          <h3>1. Peanut Butter Banana Oat Bowl</h3>
          <p><strong>Why it works:</strong> Warm, soft, filling, and easy on the stomach.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>1 cup cooked oats</li>
            <li>1 banana, sliced</li>
            <li>1 tablespoon peanut butter</li>
            <li>Handful of blueberries</li>
            <li>Sprinkle of chopped nuts or seeds</li>
          </ul>
          <div class="instructions">
            <h4>Instructions</h4>
            <p>
              Cook oats according to package directions. Top with banana, blueberries, peanut butter,
              and a sprinkle of nuts or seeds. Serve warm.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="recipe-card">
          <h3>2. Avocado Toast with Egg</h3>
          <p><strong>Why it works:</strong> Protein + healthy fats + toast for a balanced start.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>1 slice whole grain toast</li>
            <li>½ avocado, mashed</li>
            <li>1 cooked egg</li>
            <li>Few cherry tomatoes on the side</li>
            <li>Pinch of salt and pepper</li>
          </ul>
          <div class="instructions">
            <h4>Instructions</h4>
            <p>
              Toast bread. Spread mashed avocado on top. Add cooked egg and season lightly.
              Serve with tomatoes.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="recipe-card">
          <h3>3. Berry Yogurt Smoothie</h3>
          <p><strong>Why it works:</strong> Great for mornings when chewing feels hard.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>1 cup Greek yogurt</li>
            <li>1 cup frozen berries</li>
            <li>½ banana</li>
            <li>1 tablespoon chia seeds</li>
            <li>½ to 1 cup milk of choice</li>
          </ul>
          <div class="instructions">
            <h4>Instructions</h4>
            <p>
              Blend everything until smooth. Add more milk for a thinner texture. Serve cold.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="recipe-card">
          <h3>4. Yogurt Bowl with Berries & Granola</h3>
          <p><strong>Why it works:</strong> Fast, high-protein, and no cooking needed.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>1 cup Greek yogurt</li>
            <li>Fresh strawberries or raspberries</li>
            <li>¼ cup granola</li>
            <li>Optional drizzle of honey</li>
          </ul>
          <div class="instructions">
            <h4>Instructions</h4>
            <p>
              Spoon yogurt into a bowl. Add berries and granola on top. Finish with a small drizzle
              of honey if desired.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="recipe-card">
          <h3>5. Egg Muffins with Avocado</h3>
          <p><strong>Why it works:</strong> Meal-prep friendly and easy to grab on the go.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>4 eggs</li>
            <li>¼ cup chopped spinach</li>
            <li>2 tablespoons diced peppers or carrots</li>
            <li>Salt and pepper</li>
            <li>Sliced avocado for serving</li>
          </ul>
          <div class="instructions">
            <h4>Instructions</h4>
            <p>
              Whisk eggs with veggies and seasoning. Pour into a greased muffin tin and bake at
              350°F until set, about 18–20 minutes. Serve with avocado.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="recipe-card">
          <h3>6. Nut Butter Toast with Strawberries</h3>
          <p><strong>Why it works:</strong> Simple, satisfying, and quick enough for hectic mornings.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>1 slice toast</li>
            <li>1 to 2 tablespoons almond or peanut butter</li>
            <li>Sliced strawberries</li>
            <li>Optional sprinkle of chia or flax</li>
          </ul>
          <div class="instructions">
            <h4>Instructions</h4>
            <p>
              Toast bread, spread with nut butter, and top with strawberries and seeds if using.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>

      <section class="notes">
        <h3>Important Notes</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Try to include <strong>protein</strong> in breakfast to help you stay full longer.</li>
          <li>Adding <strong>fiber</strong> can support digestion and help with blood sugar balance.</li>
          <li>For nausea mornings, cold foods or smoothies may feel easier than hot meals.</li>
          <li>Keep a few <strong>low-effort options</strong> ready for days when energy is low.</li>
          <li>You can swap ingredients based on preference, tolerance, or what sounds good that day.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="chef-notes">
        <h3>Chef Tips for Making These Better</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Use ripe fruit for natural sweetness so you need less added sugar.</li>
          <li>Prep ingredients the night before to make mornings easier.</li>
          <li>Batch-make egg muffins and refrigerate for quick breakfasts during the week.</li>
          <li>For extra calories and fullness, add nut butter, seeds, avocado, or full-fat yogurt.</li>
          <li>For a prettier Pinterest-friendly presentation, use white dishes, fresh fruit, and natural light.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

